      "content": "Here's a revised template that still maintains a professional tone but with a bit more personality:\n\nSubject: Update on Senior Developer Position\n\nHey [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out and thank you again for taking the time to chat with us about the Senior Developer role at [Company Name]. We were really impressed by your skills, experience, and passion for software development - it's clear you're a talented developer who's not afraid to get their hands dirty.\n\nUnfortunately, after careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience are a better fit for our current needs. Please know that this decision wasn't made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the possibility of having you join our team.\n\nWe loved your energy and enthusiasm during the interview process, and we think you'd be a great fit for a company that values creativity, collaboration, and a willingness to take risks. We're not saying you're not a great fit for us, but rather that we're looking for someone who can help us tackle some of the challenges we're facing right now.\n\nIf you're still interested in exploring opportunities with us, I'd be happy to set up a follow-up conversation to discuss how we can work together in the future",
