      "content": "thanks, i like the tone of this one. it feels a lot more natural. \n\ni have a follow up though. sometimes when we're making these decisions, it's not even about the technical skills—it's more about the \"vibe\" of the person. like, they might be a genius, but they just don't feel like they belong in our specific little community or way of doing things. \n\nif i wanted to explain that \"lack of fit\" or that \"missing piece\" in a way that sounds empathetic rather than just saying \"we didn't like your personality,\" how would you suggest doing that? i want to be honest about the cultural aspect without being rude or condescending.",
